 of newborn calves derived from in vitro produced embryos cultured with or without serum and oviduct epithelium cells</article-title><source>Theriogenology</source><year>2000</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>147</fpage><lpage>158</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10990356</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0093-691X(00)00333-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jacobsen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmidt</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Holm</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sangild</surname><given-names>PT</given-names></name><name><surname>Vajta</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Greve</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Callesen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Body dimensions and birth and organ weights of calves derived from in vitro produced embryos cultured with or without serum and oviduct epithelium cells</article-title><source>Theriogenology</source><year>2000</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>1761</fpage><lpage>1769</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10968419</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0093-691X(00)00312-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kruip</surname><given-names>TAM</given-names></name><name><surname>den Daas</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In vitro produced and cloned embryos: Effects on pregnancy, parturition and offspring</article-title><source>Theriogenology</source><year>1997</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0093-691X(96)00338-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lazar</surname>